# Paths excluded from the RSA agents' copy of the repository (rsync
# --exclude-from). Used by stage_code.sh (agent_src) and build_agent_tree.sh
# (each cell's tree), enforced by check_agent_tree.sh before any agent starts,
# and tested by tests/test_rsa_slurm_scripts.py.
#
# Starts from scripts/subjective_randomness/slurm/agent_tree.exclude (every
# rule that applies here), plus what the RSA sweep must withhold: the real
# data (it holds the held-out rows), the code that splits, simulates and
# scores, and everything outside src/. The agents need only src/ (their
# self-check, `uv run python -m src.rsa.loop.check_candidate`, imports
# src.rsa.loop and what it imports), .here, opencode.json and pyproject.toml.
# A leading / anchors a rule at the repo root; a rule without one matches a
# name at any depth.

# --- VCS, build artefacts, caches (as subjective randomness) ---------------------
.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.nc
node_modules
.uv_cache
.pip_cache
.cache
.hf
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
# opencode's per-agent state from local runs (and its git snapshots)
.xdg_data

# --- data: every directory named data, at any depth ------------------------------
# /data/ (downloads in data/rsa/external, smoke-test outputs, earlier runs) and
# the committed real trials in src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/rsa_reference/data/
# (pragmods, Mayn & Demberg 2026, Sikos 2021 and their reference tables). The
# committed trials include the rows the split holds out, so an agent that read
# them would see the test set. The agents get their cell's train.csv only, as
# the loop's results/responses.csv.
data
# Named too, so the intent survives an edit of the rule above.
/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/rsa_reference/data/

# --- the RSA experiment build: nothing a candidate agent needs -------------------
/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/rsa_reference/experiment/
# The jsPsych build imports src.rsa.ingest (excluded below), so it would not
# even import in the tree.
/src/rsa/experiment/

# --- harness-only RSA code: ingestion, the split, simulation, scoring ------------
# The split names which conditions are held out (and with the seed, rebuilds
# them); simulate/recovery/evaluate_heldout are the evaluation side.
/src/rsa/ingest/
/src/rsa/pragmods_ingest.py
/src/rsa/split.py
/src/rsa/simulate.py
/src/rsa/recovery.py
/src/rsa/evaluate_heldout.py

# --- instruction files agent CLIs load into every session ------------------------
# (claude: CLAUDE.md; codex and opencode: AGENTS.md.) The project CLAUDE.md
# describes the evaluation; a candidate agent's brief is self-contained.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# --- everything but src/ (as subjective randomness) ------------------------------
# Docs, tests and scripts describe the split, the recovery ground truths and
# the Slurm layout (this file included).
/docs/
/tests/
/scripts/
/analysis/
/diagrams/
/README.md
/SUMMARY.md
/HERO_RUN_DESIDERATA.md
# Credentials: the agents get only their own login, from the sandbox's
# environment allowlist.
.secrets
.secrets.example

# --- subjective randomness's held-out material (not this sweep's; no RSA agent needs it)
ground_truth_models.py
evaluate_recovery.py
test_literature_faithful_pymc.py
test_literature_model_families.py
gt.txt
REFACTOR_NOTES.md
preprocess.py
/src/subjective_randomness/
/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/*/references/
/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/*/instruction_literature.md
/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/*/problem_definition.md
/src/pipelines/outer_loop/projects/*/seed_models/archive_*/
